# Product Requirements

This document defines the minimum quality standards for products submitted to the Codexeron Marketplace.

All products must comply with these requirements before they can be approved and published.

---

# General Requirements

Every product must:

- Be complete and functional.
- Be developed by the seller or legally licensed for distribution.
- Match its description and screenshots.
- Be ready for production use.
- Be free from malicious code.
- Comply with all Codexeron Marketplace policies.

---

# Code Quality

Products should follow accepted software development practices.

Your code should be:

- Clean
- Readable
- Well-structured
- Maintainable
- Properly formatted
- Free from unnecessary files

Avoid:

- Obfuscated code
- Dead code
- Hardcoded credentials
- Debug code
- Unused libraries

---

# Documentation

Every product must include documentation.

Documentation should explain:

- Installation
- Configuration
- Requirements
- Features
- Usage
- Update instructions

Well-written documentation improves the user experience.

---

# Product Files

Products should include only files required for proper operation.

Typical files include:

- Source Code
- Documentation
- License Information
- Changelog
- Installation Guide

Do not include unnecessary files.

---

# Security

Products must follow security best practices.

Products must not:

- Contain malware
- Collect personal information without consent
- Include hidden functionality
- Expose sensitive credentials
- Contain known security vulnerabilities

Security issues may result in immediate rejection.

---

# Compatibility

Product descriptions should clearly state:

- Supported PHP version
- Supported framework
- Supported database
- Required extensions
- Required server software

Compatibility information must remain accurate.

---

# Product Versioning

Every release must include a version number.

Recommended format:

```
v1.0.0
v1.0.1
v1.1.0
v2.0.0
```

A changelog should accompany each new version.

---

# Third-Party Components

If your product includes third-party libraries or dependencies:

- Ensure redistribution is permitted.
- Comply with all applicable licenses.
- Clearly identify included components.
- Credit original authors where required.

---

# Artificial Intelligence

Products created with the assistance of AI are permitted.

However:

- The seller remains fully responsible for the product.
- AI-generated code must be reviewed before submission.
- Products must meet the same quality and security standards as manually written code.

---

# Reasons for Rejection

Products may be rejected if they:

- Are incomplete
- Contain security issues
- Include poor documentation
- Misrepresent functionality
- Violate copyright or licensing rules
- Fail to meet quality standards

---

# Best Practices

To improve approval chances:

- Test your product before submission.
- Keep documentation up to date.
- Use semantic versioning.
- Follow secure coding practices.
- Provide clear product descriptions.

